Copies of the files agents show in the chat, kept by the server.

The web UI loads a file a reply shows with image syntax from the session's
sandbox (web-patches/0033-inline-media.patch), so an asleep or deleted
sandbox, such as an archived session's, left a grey chip in its place.
omnigent_chat_media (images/server/omnigent_chat_media.py) keeps a copy of
each such file in the artifact store, and omnigent_chat_media_api, mounted
here, serves GET /v1/sessions/{id}/chat-media?path=<path as the reply wrote
it>: from the sandbox while it can be reached, refreshing the copy, and from
the copy otherwise. A file outside the workspace is owner-only, as in the
file viewer.

_publish_status reports each change of a session's status to
omnigent_chat_media.on_status. When a turn ends (idle or failed), the
session's newest replies are scanned and every file they show without a copy
as new as the reply is fetched and kept, so a reply nobody looked at while
the sandbox ran still has its images. Deleting a session deletes its copies.

